---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import "../styles/legal.css";

const updated = "27 October 2026";
---

<Base
	title="GDPR compliance"
	description="How LibertAI applies the GDPR: minimised data, legal bases, data subject rights, processors, transfers and security. A European company, European hosting."
	path="/gdpr"
	alt="/rgpd"
	lang="en"
>
	<section class="legal-page">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="doc">
				<a class="back" href="/">← libertai.io</a>
				<h1>GDPR compliance</h1>
				<div class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</div>

				<div class="note">
					<p style="margin:0">
						<strong>English translation.</strong> This page is a translation provided for information only. The French version
						at <a href="/rgpd">/rgpd</a> is the reference text.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="toc">
					<a href="#commitment">Our commitment</a>
					<a href="#principle">Minimisation</a>
					<a href="#bases">Legal bases</a>
					<a href="#rights">Your rights</a>
					<a href="#processors">Processors</a>
					<a href="#transfers">Transfers</a>
					<a href="#security">Security</a>
					<a href="#trackers">Trackers</a>
					<a href="#companies">Companies</a>
					<a href="#authority">Supervisory authority</a>
					<a href="#contact">Contact</a>
					<a href="#changes">Changes</a>
				</div>

				<h2 id="commitment">1. Our commitment</h2>
				<p>
					The data controller is <strong>Intelligence Artificielle Générale SAS</strong> (“LibertAI”), 76 Promenade des Anglais,
					94210 Saint-Maur-des-Fossés, France — SIREN 985 392 356.
				</p>
				<p>
					LibertAI is a European company, subject to the GDPR for all of its processing: website, chat, API, console, agents
					and related services. Data protection is not a layer added afterwards: it is the product. Our technical choices — no
					content retention, no training on your data, verifiable infrastructure — follow directly from the principles of
					minimisation and data protection by design (Art. 25 GDPR).
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Minimised data</strong>: we collect only what the service and billing require.</li>
					<li><strong>No content stored</strong>: prompts and responses are not recorded in a database.</li>
					<li><strong>No training</strong>: your data is never used to train, tune or evaluate a model.</li>
					<li><strong>No resale</strong>: your data is never sold, rented or traded.</li>
					<li><strong>No advertising</strong>: no advertising cookies, no social pixels, no marketing profiling.</li>
					<li><strong>European hosting</strong>: our hosting provider, Aleph.IM SAS, is established in Paris, France.</li>
					<li><strong>Exercisable rights</strong>: one address, an answer within one month.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 id="principle">2. Processing kept to a minimum</h2>
				<p>
					In practice, here is what we process and what we do not. This summary mirrors the privacy policy, which is the
					authoritative text.
				</p>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>We process</th><th>We do not process</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Account, email or wallet address, sessions and API keys</td>
							<td>The content of your conversations and requests, in a database</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Usage counters: tokens, images, model called, timestamp</td>
							<td>Your bank card data, which never passes through our servers</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Payment references and accounting records</td>
							<td>Advertising profiling or a browsing history sold on</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Limited technical logs, for security and diagnostics</td>
							<td>An IP address linked to an account in our databases</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<p>
					IP addresses are used transiently, in memory, to limit abuse and determine the display currency. Like any online
					service, our servers and load balancers produce technical logs that may contain IP addresses; these are retained
					for a limited period, solely for security and diagnostic purposes.
				</p>

				<h2 id="bases">3. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
				<p>
					Each processing operation relies on an identified legal basis under Article 6 of the GDPR. No processing relies on
					consent where the service cannot work without it: in that case, the basis is performance of the contract.
				</p>
				<table>
					<thead>
						<tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<td>Account creation and management, provision of the service</td>
							<td>Performance of the contract — Art. 6(1)(b)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Billing, subscriptions, accounting</td>
							<td>Performance of the contract and legal obligation — Art. 6(1)(b) and 6(1)(c)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Security, abuse prevention, rate limiting</td>
							<td>Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f)</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td>Aggregated audience measurement</td>
							<td>Legitimate interest — Art. 6(1)(f), without individual profiling</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
				<p>
					Retention periods, recipients and the detail of the data processed are described in the
					<a href="/privacy-policy#finalites">privacy policy</a>.
				</p>

				<h2 id="rights">4. Your rights</h2>
				<p>You have the following rights, across all processing:</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>access</strong> to your data and to information about how it is processed;</li>
					<li><strong>rectification</strong> of inaccurate or incomplete data;</li>
					<li><strong>erasure</strong> of your data, subject to statutory retention obligations;</li>
					<li><strong>restriction</strong> of processing;</li>
					<li><strong>portability</strong> of the data you provided to us;</li>
					<li><strong>objection</strong> to processing based on our legitimate interest, on grounds relating to your particular situation;</li>
					<li><strong>withdrawal of consent</strong> at any time, where processing is based on consent;</li>
					<li>
						<strong>post-mortem directives</strong> on what happens to your data, in accordance with Article 85 of the French
						Data Protection Act.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					To exercise these rights, write to <a href="mailto:privacy@libertai.io">privacy@libertai.io</a>. We respond within
					one month, extendable by two months for complex requests. We may ask you for the information needed to verify that
					the request does come from you.
				</p>
				<p>
					Certain data cannot be erased: accounting records, which the law requires us to retain, and transactions recorded
					on a public blockchain, which are technically immutable.
				</p>

				<h2 id="processors">5. Processors</h2>
				<p>
					We use identified providers, each for a specific purpose and acting on our instructions. Hosting and confidential
					computing infrastructure are provided by <strong>Aleph.IM SAS</strong>, established in Paris. The other providers —
					payments, sign-in via Google or GitHub, email delivery, geolocation for currency and VAT, self-hosted audience
					measurement — are listed in the
					<a href="/privacy-policy#destinataires">privacy policy</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					None of these providers uses your data for advertising. When your browser contacts one of them, that service
					technically receives your IP address, as with any resource loaded from a third-party domain.
				</p>

				<h2 id="transfers">6. Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
				<p>
					Some providers are established outside the European Union, in particular in the United States. These transfers are
					covered by the appropriate safeguards provided for in Chapter V of the GDPR, in particular the European
					Commission's standard contractual clauses.
				</p>
				<p>
					Crypto-asset payments are recorded on public blockchains, accessible worldwide and immutable by nature. This
					publicity is inherent to the technology and beyond our control.
				</p>

				<h2 id="security">7. Security</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>encryption of data in transit (HTTPS);</li>
					<li>encryption at rest of sensitive authentication tokens;</li>
					<li>storage of session tokens and sign-in codes as irreversible hashes;</li>
					<li>authentication cookie inaccessible to the page's JavaScript (<span class="mono">httpOnly</span>), transmitted over HTTPS only;</li>
					<li>cryptographic verification of notifications from our payment providers;</li>
					<li>
						execution of certain models in a hardware-attested trusted execution environment (TEE), indicated model by
						model in the interface.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Minimisation is our first security measure: less data retained means less data to protect. How attestation works
					is described in the
					<a href="https://docs.libertai.io/concepts/trust-model.html" rel="noopener" target="_blank">trust model</a>.
				</p>

				<h2 id="trackers">8. Trackers and consent</h2>
				<p>
					The website and applications set only trackers strictly necessary for the service: session, protection of
					sign-in via Google or GitHub, routing continuity and the state of the side panel. These trackers do not require
					consent.
				</p>
				<p>
					Audience measurement is provided by a <strong>self-hosted solution, without advertising cookies and without
					cross-site tracking</strong>. The data is strictly statistical, is not cross-referenced with other processing and
					is not shared with any third party. It therefore falls within the consent exemption provided by the CNIL for
					audience measurement. The list of cookies is in the
					<a href="/privacy-policy#traceurs">privacy policy</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>No advertising cookies, no social network pixels and no third-party behavioural trackers</strong> are set.
					That is why the website shows no consent banner.
				</p>

				<h2 id="companies">9. Companies and data processing</h2>
				<p>
					For business customers, LibertAI contracts as a European company and issues a European invoice. On request, we
					provide:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>a <strong>data processing agreement</strong> (DPA) compliant with Article 28 of the GDPR;</li>
					<li>the <strong>list of processors</strong> and the applicable transfer safeguards;</li>
					<li>the <strong>security documentation</strong> and attestation material for confidential environments;</li>
					<li>answers to your <strong>security and compliance questionnaires</strong>.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					To start these conversations: <a href="mailto:contact@libertai.io">contact@libertai.io</a>.
				</p>

				<h2 id="authority">10. Supervisory authority</h2>
				<p>
					If, after contacting us, you believe your rights are not being respected, you may lodge a complaint with the
					<strong>Commission nationale de l'informatique et des libertés (CNIL)</strong>, 3 place de Fontenoy, TSA 80715,
					75334 Paris Cedex 07 — <a href="https://www.cnil.fr" rel="noopener" target="_blank">cnil.fr</a>.
				</p>

				<h2 id="contact">11. Contact</h2>
				<dl>
					<dt>Personal data and rights</dt>
					<dd><a href="mailto:privacy@libertai.io">privacy@libertai.io</a></dd>
					<dt>General and business enquiries</dt>
					<dd><a href="mailto:contact@libertai.io">contact@libertai.io</a></dd>
					<dt>Data controller</dt>
					<dd>Intelligence Artificielle Générale SAS, 76 Promenade des Anglais, 94210 Saint-Maur-des-Fossés, France</dd>
				</dl>
				<p>
					Related documents: <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>,
					<a href="/legal-notices">legal notices</a>, <a href="/terms">terms of sale</a>.
				</p>

				<h2 id="changes">12. Changes</h2>
				<p>
					This page may be updated to reflect a change in our processing or in the regulations. The date at the top
					indicates the latest revision; in the event of a substantial change, users with an account will be informed.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<Footer lang="en" variant="legal" />
</Base>
